# eoreader6.1 · kernel · turn 033 — REFUSED, not earned
# Attempted act: SIG*  (Signal aimed at Pattern)   Stance: Tracing   Site: Kind
#
# turn-005 already earned SIG* — for the "absent"/"present" kind. This is
# a SEPARATE attempt, for the NEW "anomalous"/"ordinary" kind turn-32 just
# bound. Earning one kind's Pattern-grain use does not earn another's; the
# cell is the same address, but the claim is about a different recurrence,
# and each recurrence must be checked on its own material — exactly what
# Amendment I, ported since gap-002's very first note, requires: a license
# earned for one pair carries no warrant for another.
#
# Checked and genuinely absent: turn-32 binds "anomalous" to exactly ONE
# entity (signal-c-outlier's candidate). There is no second, independently
# generated anomalous instance to trace consistency across. The sixth
# refusal of this shape overall, and the first to recur at an ALREADY-
# EARNED cell rather than a new one — worth naming as its own small
# finding: earning SIG* once does not make SIG* free everywhere in the
# grid. Each kind still has to bring its own recurrence.
#
# What would earn it: a second, independently-generated series with its
# own magnitude anomaly at a comparable site-role — not this same outlier
# reread, and not one invented solely to close this cell.

:gap-033  eot:opens        :turn-32 .
:gap-033  eot:attempted    eot:SIG* .
:gap-033  eot:for_kind     "anomalous" .
:gap-033  eot:refused      true .
:gap-033  eot:reason       "insufficient_recurrence_for_this_kind" .
:gap-033  eot:witnessed    false .
